:: R3_Choice_Shame [r3 story]
<<modstat "submission" 8>>
<<modstat "victoriaTrust" 3>>
<<npc "victoria" "trust" 3>>
<<objective "Leave Victoria's office.">>

<<sayself>>Yes, Ms. Cross.<</sayself>>

The words come out dry. Quiet. They taste like copper pennies.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>Good boy.<</say>>

Two words. They hit somewhere below my stomach and above my cock. A location I don't have a map for. A part of the body that medical textbooks don't chart because it only exists in moments like this, when someone with authority says something that shouldn't feel like what it feels like.

My face is burning. My neck is burning. The panties are a warm knot of silk in my fist and my knuckles are white around them and I don't know what I feel. I know what I should feel. I should feel revolted, offended, ready to stand up and walk out and call HR and retain a lawyer. That is what the man my father raised would do. That man would be on his feet already.

That man is sitting very still.

I take the panties because I have no choice. That's what I tell myself. That's the story I construct in the elevator going down. Forty-two floors of narrative building. I am a man who was cornered. A man who did what he had to do. Survival. Pragmatism. The calculated surrender of someone playing a long game.

The fabric in my pocket means nothing. It's a transaction. A cost of doing business. The same as a handshake I don't want to give or a dinner I don't want to attend. Corporate reality.

I repeat this in my head for the rest of the day. By 5 PM I almost believe it.

Almost.

