:: R3_VictoriaFarewell [r3 story]
<<location "Victoria Cross's Office, Floor 42">>

Victoria returns to her side of the desk. Sits down in her higher chair. The power geometry reasserts itself. She opens her laptop like we've been discussing quarterly projections.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>Tomorrow. Under your suit. All day. You can go.<</say>>

She types something. Doesn't look up.

I stand. The panties are still in my hand. I fold them. A small, precise fold, the way I fold my pocket square on Sunday nights. Muscle memory from a ritual designed to project control. I tuck them into my jacket pocket. The inside pocket, against my chest, where I keep my wallet and my phone and now this.

The weight is negligible. A few grams of silk and lace. It feels like carrying a grenade with the pin half-pulled.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>Daniel.<</say>>

I stop at the door. Turn.

Victoria is looking at me. Her expression has shifted by a degree. Still composed, still certain, but there's something warmer in it now. Something proprietary. The look of a woman who just acquired something she intends to keep.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>You made the right choice.<</say>>

I nod. Open the door. Walk out.

